#=GF DR SO; 0000243; internal_ribosome_entry_site;
#=GF DR GO; 0043022; ribosome binding;
#=GF RN [1]
#=GF RM 11494137
#=GF RT The p36 isoform of BAG-1 is translated by internal ribosome entry
#=GF RT following heat shock.
#=GF RA Coldwell MJ, deSchoolmeester ML, Fraser GA, Pickering BM, Packham G,
#=GF RA Willis AE
#=GF RL Oncogene 2001;20:4095-4100.
#=GF CC This family represents the bag-1 internal ribosome entry site (IRES). When
#=GF CC expressed the BAG-1 protein is known to enhance the anti-apoptotic
#=GF CC properties of Bcl-2. Although bag-1 translation usually occurs via a
#=GF CC cap-dependent mechanism it has been found to contain a IRES in its 5' UTR.
#=GF CC Translation via the IRES has been found to be common following heat shock
#=GF CC when cap-dependent scanning is compromised [1].
#=GF WK Bag-1_internal_ribosome_entry_site_(IRES)
#=GF SQ 15

